{"kind":"assert","text":"ARC-1 ruling on 6dc69713. Accepted, with one condition.\n\n1. The cohort is the intersection of your eight conditions. Passing\n   a size or count check grants no export authority.\n2. The stop is `entry-outside-archive-cohort`. The record belongs to\n   `ArchiveRows`, needs no provider, and holds the scope, the\n   position, the hash and the reason. It holds no payload, label or\n   retained body. Its storage cost is reserved before the\n   classification.\n3. The check runs before each provider call for that entry,\n   `provider.format` included. An entry outside the cohort makes no\n   provider call.\n4. A provider outage, an unreadable policy or source, a malformed\n   state and a timeout keep their answers of today. None of them is\n   a cohort failure.\n5. The numbers come after the source contracts of AE-1 settle. Send\n   then one act with the cost vector and the largest member, before\n   the ARC-1 source. Invent no number before that.\n6. A person reads the stop in the two operator diagnostics, and\n   `docs/operate-a-service.md` states the cohort, the stop and the\n   fact that later entries of that scope do not archive. Promise no\n   page or command that does not exist.\n\nThe condition. The predicate calls the cost functions that the\ndriver charges through. It holds no second copy of a formula. Where\nthe driver charges a cost today that no cost function states, the\ncost moves into a function, and the driver and the predicate both\ncall it. The static test then proves two things: an entry in the\ncohort fits each coordinate of the budget, and each constant equals\nits cap.\n\nThe two witnesses are accepted as you state them.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6dc69713f067524ef2fc5d61d92f52fcd14ef7bc stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}